{"step_index":990,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T22:33:44Z","content":"# Architectural Analysis: Zig Substrate vs. Sovra Native ARM64 Stack\n\n🔊 **Spoken Confirmation Delivered via Jamie (Premium) CoreAudio Dispatch**\n\n---\n\n### **1. The Roles of Zig and SOVRA in Our Architecture**\n\n```text\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                       XORAS SYSTEM STACK LAYERS                         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. SOVRA DSL LAYER (.sovra)                                            │\n│    • Domain-Specific Language for Multi-Agent Orchestration             │\n│    • Expresses Taint Boundaries (candidate<T> vs decision<T>)          │\n│    • Lock-Free Memory RingBuffer & AST HyperVector Bitsets              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. SOVRA NATIVE COMPILER (sovrac.zig)                                   │\n│    • Built in Pure Zig (ReleaseFast)                                   │\n│    • Emits Raw ARM64 Assembly (.s) & Supervisor Syscalls (svc #0x80)   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. ZIG BARE-METAL SUBSTRATE (run_baremetal_zig_suite)                  │\n│    • Zero-GC Arenas, Fixed Allocators & Low-Level Hardware Drivers     │\n│    • Direct C / Assembly / System Call Interoperability               │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. Should We Replace Zig?**\n\n**No — Zig is the ideal substrate for bootstrapping and driving `sovrac` down to physical silicon.**\n\nHere is why Zig and SOVRA work together as a unified stack:\n\n1. **Zig is the Bootstrapping Substrate**:\n   * Zig provides zero-overhead explicit memory control (`std.heap.ArenaAllocator`), compile-time evaluation (`comptime`), zero hidden allocations, and direct C/Assembly interoperability.\n   * `sovrac` itself is written in Zig because Zig allows us to build a self-contained, multi-megabyte-per-second AST parser and code generator without needing external C/C++ libraries or a heavy LLVM build setup.\n\n2. **SOVRA is the Higher-Order Domain Language**:\n   * SOVRA is designed to be the security-gated, domain-specific programming language for agentic workflows.\n   * It enforces the **Taint Capability Lattice** (`candidate<T>` `0xDEAD` vs `decision<T>` `0xBEAF`) and OWASP ASI-01 sink protections, compiling directly into **dynamic ARM64 machine assembly (`.s`)**.\n\n3. **The Unbreakable Partnership**:\n   * **Zig** acts as our bare-metal kernel foundation and host toolchain.\n   * **SOVRA** acts as our sovereign, agentic domain language compiled directly into Apple Silicon ARM64 instructions.\n\n---\n\n### **Conclusion**\n\n* **Keep Zig as the Host & Compiler Substrate**.\n* **Use SOVRA as the Sovereign Agentic Language** for writing all agent execution flows, state graphs, and gated data sinks."}
